94|   What this is: `JSON.stringify("lectoria.theme")` renders
95|   `"lectoria.theme"`, so the evaluated string equals the old literal
96|   (verified by comparing the old file's script against the interpolated
97|   reconstruction in node: identical). `initialTheme` untouched;
98|   `chrome.tsx:7` re-exports, so `reader.tsx` (still importing from chrome)
99|   needed no edit and keeps working. New theme tests evaluate the script
100|   with null, "garbage", "dark", "light", and a throwing localStorage, all
101|   resolving as specified.
102|10. Tests are meaningful (`app/folio/figure-placement.test.ts:1-105`,
103|    `app/theme.test.ts:18-48`).
104|    Placement: insertion order per endN, whole paragraph, last-fragment-only
105|    on one page, both-pages split (documents current behavior, does not
106|    change it), multi-figure, none, found/later-page/missing ordinal. Gates:
107|    scene-blocks-figure and vice versa, finish releases, retry refused from
